  "conclusion": "NUANCED NULL for g_t: At h=22d (monthly), VIX-only achieves OOS R2=+5.63% with CW=+2.02 (p=0.021), but g_t-only achieves only R2=+0.87% (CW=0.91, p=0.183, not significant). g_t adds NO incremental value beyond VIX for return prediction. The monthly predictability comes from VIX level, not from A4f's GARCH dynamics (g_t). At h=1d and h=5d, all models fail (negative R2). This extends K818 (SSVS null) and K998 (g_t cannot predict VRP). In-sample, VRP shows significant t-stats (2.68-3.46), but this does not survive OOS. The long-short strategy based on g_t yields negative Sharpe (-0.12 to -0.07 vs BH 0.71-0.77), confirming no economic value from g_t signal."
